\id PSA - Berean Standard Bible
\h Psalm
\toc1 Psalms
\toc2 Psalm
\toc3 Psalm
\mt1 Psalms
\c 23
\s1 The LORD Is My Shepherd
\r (Ezekiel 34:11–24; John 10:1–21)
\d A Psalm of David.
\q1
\v 1 The LORD is my shepherd;\f + \fr 23:1 \ft See \+xt Revelation 7:17\+xt*.\f*
\q2 I shall not want.
\q1
\v 2 He makes me lie down in green pastures;
\q2 He leads me beside quiet waters.
\q1
\v 3 He restores my soul;
\q2 He guides me in the paths of righteousness
\q2 for the sake of His name.
\q1
\v 4 Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,\f + \fr 23:4 \ft Or the valley of deep darkness\f*
\q2 I will fear no evil,
\q1 for You are with me;
\q2 Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me.
\b
\q1
\v 5 You prepare a table before me
\q2 in the presence of my enemies.
\q1 You anoint my head with oil;
\q2 my cup overflows.
\q1
\v 6 Surely goodness and mercy will follow me
\q2 all the days of my life,
\q1 and I will dwell in the house of the LORD
\q2 forever\f + \fr 23:6 \ft Literally for a length of days\f*.
